## Hints

- E2: Welch SE = sqrt(sM²/nM + sO²/nO) where O = the other 4 days
  pooled (they are one group for this contrast).
- E3: on synthetic data, the sub-period "discoveries" are the
  multiplicity lottery made visible — count how many blocks would have
  been "significant" at 5%.
- E4: 52 events/year; cost is per event, so annualize both the edge
  and the cost by the same 52.
